course: dictionary
lesson: 11539
title: Alternation: one thing, then another
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Alternation is when two things take turns, one after the other, again and again. It comes from the word alternate, which means taking turns. «The alternation of day and night gives us a new morning every twenty-four hours.» First day, then night, then day again.
explain: Look for the pattern: what comes first, what comes next, and does it repeat? In «red, blue, red, blue, red», the colours alternate. Alternation is the name for that repeating turn-taking.
explain: Alternation is a noun, so you can have one alternation or many alternations. You can also say the alternation of two things, such as «the alternation of hot and cold weather in spring».
fact: Alternation means the pattern of one thing following another again and again.
fact: Alternation is a noun. Its plural is alternations.
fact: In maths, 1, 2, 1, 2 is an alternating pattern.
fact: In science, the alternation of day and night, of seasons, and of tides follows a repeating pattern.
fact: In poetry, the alternation of strong and weak beats gives a poem its rhythm.
exercise: Which of these is an example of alternation? | A ball that bounces once and stops | A cup filled once and left empty | *Day, then night, then day again | One loud shout and then silence
exercise: «The tides show a steady alternation of high and low water.» What does alternation mean? | *A pattern of one thing following another again and again | A sudden stop | One very large wave, only once | A mess of things all at once
exercise: «The alternation of red and blue made a bright band across the wall.» Which word names the pattern of colours taking turns? | band | wall | bright | *alternation
exercise: Nadia says, «Alternation is just another word for mixing things up.» What is the better answer? | Alternation means one thing that never changes | Alternation means a loud noise | *Alternation means a pattern that repeats, with one thing following another | Alternation means throwing everything together at random
test: What does «regular alternation» mean? | A broken rule | A sudden surprise | A kind of loud music | *A steady pattern that repeats
test: Which is an example of alternation in poetry? | Lines with no beat at all | A poem with no rhythm | *Strong and weak beats taking turns | One very long word
exam: Which of these shows alternation best? | *Spring, summer, autumn, winter, then spring again | A stone sitting still all year | One loud bang and then silence | A single sunny afternoon
